      "external_key": "q-geometry-right-triangles-finding-a-leg",
      "topic": "Right Triangles",
      "subtopic": "Finding a leg",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "A right triangle has hypotenuse ${{k*13}}$ and one leg ${{k*5}}$. Find the other leg.",
      "answer": "${{k*12}}$",
      "solution": "$({{k*13}})^2 - ({{k*5}})^2 = {{k*k*169}} - {{k*k*25}} = {{k*k*144}}$, so the other leg is $\\sqrt{ {{k*k*144}} } = {{k*12}}$.",
      "tags": [
