      "topic": "Right Triangles",
      "subtopic": "Trigonometric ratios",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "In a right triangle, the side opposite angle $\\theta$ is ${{a}}$ and the hypotenuse is ${{c}}$. Find $\\sin\\theta$, and then $\\theta$ to the nearest degree.",
      "answer": "$\\sin\\theta = {{frac(a,c)}}$, so $\\theta \\approx {{fmt(asin(a/c) * 180 / pi, 0)}}^\\circ$",
      "solution": "$\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = {{frac(a,c)}}$. Taking the inverse sine gives $\\theta \\approx {{fmt(asin(a/c) * 180 / pi, 0)}}$ degrees.",
      "tags": [
