      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "A tangent touches a circle of radius ${{k*3}}$ at point $T$. The tangent meets a point $P$ with $OP = {{k*5}}$, where $O$ is the centre. Find $PT$.",
      "answer": "${{k*4}}$",
      "solution": "A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact, so $OTP$ is a right triangle with the right angle at $T$. Then $PT = \\sqrt{ ({{k*5}})^2 - ({{k*3}})^2 } = \\sqrt{ {{k*k*16}} } = {{k*4}}$.",
